      "description": "Watch Alanyaspor vs Goztepe highlights and goals from Süper Lig on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 12, 2026. An intense Süper Lig battle unfolded on September 12, 2026 , as Alanyaspor and Göztepe clashed in a match defined by strategic shifts and clinical finishing. Both teams displayed immense energy from the opening whistle in a contest that kept fans on the edge of their seats. Alanyaspor Takes the Early Initiative The match began with Alanyaspor looking to dictate the tempo on their home turf. Their early dominance paid off in the 28th minute when Rhaldney Norberto broke the deadlock. Following a precise assist from Alexis Antunes , Norberto finished coolly to put the hosts ahead. Göztepe struggled to find their rhythm in the first half, with Juan picking up an early yellow card as the visitors found it difficult to break through a well-organized home defense. Tactical Shifts and the Turning Point The narrative of the game changed completely in the second half, largely driven by strategic substitutions from the visitors. The introduction of Ivan Cedric and Ianis Hagi in the 58th minute provided the spark Göztepe desperately needed. In the 63rd minute, the pressure told as Ivan Cedric set up Paolo Fernandes for the equalizer. The goal shifted the momentum entirely, leaving Alanyaspor struggling to regain the control they had enjoyed earlier in the match. A Twelve-Minute Blitz Silences the Hosts The match was ultimately decided by a frantic period that saw the visitors seize total control. In the 73rd minute, Göztepe were awarded a penalty, which Juan converted with clinical precision to put his side in front. Before the home side could catch their breath, they were struck again. In the 75th minute, Ianis Hagi turned provider, assisting Gaius Makouta for a third goal that effectively ended the contest. Despite late efforts from Alanyaspor to fight back, including the introduction of Bekir Boke and Ui-Jo Hwang , the visitors remained disciplined. The final whistle blew after nine minutes of stoppage time, confirming a massive away victory for Göztepe after a stunning second-half display."
