      "description": "Watch Eyüpspor vs Alanyaspor highlights and goals from Süper Lig on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 30, 2026. On August 30, 2026, the Süper Lig witnessed a captivating encounter between Eyüpspor and Alanyaspor . Both sides took to the pitch with high ambitions, setting the stage for a game filled with tactical intrigue and physical intensity. Early Shock and the Path to Recovery The match could not have started in more explosive fashion. In the very 1st minute, Alanyaspor stunned the home crowd as Arda Usluoglu found the back of the net, putting the visitors ahead before many fans had even taken their seats. This early setback forced Eyüpspor into an immediate uphill battle, placing immense pressure on the home side to find a way back into the contest under the afternoon sun. That persistence eventually paid off late in the first half. In the 39th minute, a well-worked attacking move saw Zak Jules turn provider, delivering a precise pass to Ahmed Abdullahi . The forward made no mistake, finishing clinically to level the score at 1-1. The equalizer shifted the momentum and sent both teams into the locker rooms with everything to play for in the second period. Disciplinary Battle and Tactical Shifts The second half began with a noticeable increase in physicality as both teams fought for supremacy in midfield. The referee was kept busy, issuing a series of yellow cards to maintain order. Matondo was the first Eyüpspor player cautioned in the 49th minute, while Alanyaspor 's Ümit Akdağ followed shortly after. As the tension mounted, Talha Ulvan and Charles-Andre Raux-Yao also saw yellow, reflecting the high stakes of the encounter. Managerial interventions followed as both dugouts looked to break the deadlock. Eyüpspor introduced fresh legs including Ianis Hagi and Meschack Elia , searching for that decisive creative spark. Meanwhile, Alanyaspor made their own adjustments, replacing the tiring Arda Usluoglu and Bilal Boutobba to tighten their defensive shape and look for opportunities on the counter-attack. Stoppage Time Drama As the match entered its final stages, it appeared destined for a stalemate. However, the 94th minute delivered the ultimate twist in the narrative. Zak Jules , who had already assisted the first goal, rose to the occasion to become the match-winner. He struck deep into stoppage time to make it 2-1, sparking wild celebrations across the stadium. The referee’s final whistle followed shortly after, confirming a hard-earned victory for Eyüpspor in a match defined by their refusal to settle for a draw."
